// A std container over a std specialization over a POINTER to a user class, named in a
// FILE-SCOPE SIGNATURE. The signature pre-pass now requests every nested component before the
// outer one, so std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>> binds in a signature (pinned as values in
// Test/test_cpp_interop_template.cb, section M103). This POINTER shape does not, and it is
// refused as a LOCAL too - "'std::vector<std::vector<nest::Cell *>>' does not name a C++ class
// type in the imported headers" - so this refusal says something true rather than contradicting
// a spelling that works elsewhere. Tracked by
// internal/issue/p2/cpp-nested-user-class-pointer-at-inner-depth-unresolvable.md.
//
// PIN, not a discriminator: this file passes on the pre-fix binary too.
//
// Three authoring facts measured while writing it:
//   1. expect_error matches the UNLOCALIZED format string ("unknown type '{}'"), never the
//      displayed "cannot find the type ..." text. The nested-argument refusal was reported as
//      uncatchable; it is catchable, with the source spelling.
//   2. BARE semicolon form, alone in its file. A refused file-scope signature reports TWICE -
//      the generic "unknown type" from the signature pre-pass, then the request's own message
//      from the codegen walk - so a SCOPED block is armed for both and no single expectation
//      can satisfy it. The bare form stops at the first.
//   3. It cannot live in err_cpp_nested_missing.cb: a file-scope signature is resolved before
//      main's body is walked, so a bare expectation here swallows that file's reject leg, and a
//      scoped one changes that leg's message by memoizing std::vector's owning group.
import cpp "vector" cache;
import cpp "cpp_interop_nest.h" cache;

// The accept half comes FIRST: the bare expectation below covers the rest of the file, and the
// same outer spelling one pointer level shallower has to keep binding.
int nested_ptr_ok(std.vector<nest.Cell*> v) { return (int)v.size(); }

expect_error("unknown type 'std.vector<std.vector<nest.Cell*>>'");
int nested_ptr_sig(std.vector<std.vector<nest.Cell*>> v) { return (int)v.size(); }

extern int main()
{
    nest.Cell one = nest.Cell(2, 3);
    std.vector<nest.Cell*> ok = default;
    ok.push_back(&one);
    if (nested_ptr_ok(ok) != 1) return 1;
    if (ok[0]->b != 3) return 2;
    return 0;
}
